# Vercel Web Analytics Implementation Report

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for this static HTML website project.

## Implementation Details

### Framework Identified
- **Type**: Static HTML site (no build system or package manager)
- **Files**: 10 HTML pages

### Installation Method
According to the official Vercel Analytics documentation (fetched from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart and https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/package), for static HTML sites, the analytics script is added directly to the HTML files without requiring the `@vercel/analytics` npm package.

### Changes Made

#### Added Analytics Script to All HTML Files:
The following script tag was added to the `<head>` section of all 10 HTML files:
```html
<script defer src="https://cdn.vercel-insights.com/v1/script.js"></script>
```

#### Files Modified:
1. `choix-esperluette.html` - Added analytics script
2. `index.html` - Added analytics script
3. `option1.html` - Added analytics script
4. `option2.html` - Added analytics script
5. `option3.html` - Added analytics script
6. `option4.html` - Added analytics script
7. `option5.html` - Added analytics script
8. `option6.html` - Added analytics script
9. `optionb.html` - Added analytics script
10. `optionc.html` - Added analytics script

## Implementation Choices

### Why This Approach?
1. **Static HTML Site**: The project has no package.json or build system, making it a pure static HTML site
2. **CDN-based Script**: The official Vercel documentation recommends using the CDN-hosted script (`https://cdn.vercel-insights.com/v1/script.js`) for static sites
3. **Defer Attribute**: Used `defer` to ensure the script loads after the HTML is parsed, preventing any blocking of page rendering
4. **Consistent Placement**: Added the script in the `<head>` section before the closing `</head>` tag for all files to maintain consistency

### Next Steps for Activation
To complete the Web Analytics setup, the project owner will need to:
1. Enable Web Analytics in the Vercel dashboard (Project Settings → Analytics → Enable)
2. Deploy the site to Vercel
3. Analytics data will automatically start collecting after deployment

## Verification

- ✅ All 10 HTML files contain the analytics script
- ✅ Script placement is consistent across all files
- ✅ HTML structure preserved without breaking changes
- ✅ No build errors (static site requires no build)
- ✅ All changes staged with git

## Technical Notes

- The analytics script is loaded from Vercel's CDN and will automatically track page views
- The script uses the `defer` attribute for optimal performance
- No package dependencies were added as this is a static HTML site
- No lock files to update (no package manager used)
- The script will only become active once Web Analytics is enabled in the Vercel dashboard
